FILES: examples/core/index.html, examples/core/main.js, examples/core/README.md
FEATURE: core-fixes
DATE: 2026-10-07
PRIOR STATE: as added by core-docs

OLD_SECTION
Section 07 "Bad input, and known defects": twelve throwing calls plus nine broken calls
shown failing. Page-side workarounds: #shot .mOverlay{left:0} and overflow:hidden on the
overlay host; clearing poster.style.transition after a filter pulse; try/catch around
browserType(); comments saying scroll.y() must be given true and makeActive must be
given a parent.

NEW_SECTION
Section 07 "Bad input, and repaired calls": fifteen throwing calls ($$.sav("li"),
slide.toRight({ colour }) and $$.randomString(2.5) now throw descriptive errors) and a
"Repaired in this release" row showing what the nine formerly broken calls return now
(IO.save downloads vux-demo.json). Workarounds removed; the filter pulse now uses
callBack to reset its sliders. README "techniques" section reduced to what the library
still leaves to the consumer.

REASON
The page demonstrated the defects this feature fixes; it now demonstrates the fixes.
